  "notes": "{旗|はた} refers to flags and banners. Used both literally and figuratively.\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {国旗|こっき}: national flag\n- {白旗|しらはた}: white flag (surrender)\n- {旗印|はたじるし}: banner, slogan, rallying cry\n- {赤旗|あかはた}: red flag\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {旗|はた}を{振|ふ}る: to wave a flag\n- {旗|はた}を{揚|あ}げる: to raise a flag; to start a cause\n- {旗|はた}を{掲|かか}げる: to hoist a banner\n- {旗色|はたいろ}が{悪|わる}い: things look bad (idiom)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nThe Japanese national flag is called {日の丸|ひのまる} (circle of the sun).",
